Sval: adblock-rust parses procedural cosmetic filters

Without its css-validation feature, adblock-rust returns a procedural filter
such as `:has-text(...)` or `:upward(...)` as a plain hiding selector, so its
procedural_actions are always empty and Sval's page rules never run them. The
feature asks for cssparser 0.34 and selectors 0.26. selectors 0.26 is the
in-tree servo/components/selectors, and build/rust/cssparser-0.34 (synced
from Sval's chrome/) answers 0.34 with the vendored cssparser 0.37 it is built
on, so nothing new is vendored.

